---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import iphoneDuration from "../../../video/public/iphone-duration-45.png";
import iphoneSchedules from "../../../video/public/iphone-schedules.png";
import iphoneWebsites from "../../../video/public/iphone-websites.png";
import macDuration from "../../../video/public/mac-duration-45.png";
import macSchedules from "../../../video/public/mac-schedules.png";
import macWebsites from "../../../video/public/mac-websites.png";
---

<Base description="Posato blocks the websites and apps you choose for a timed pause on your Mac, iPhone, Linux computer, or Android phone, now or on a schedule. No Posato account, no analytics, and no Posato-operated server.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <h1>A little space.<br /><span>For what matters.</span></h1>
      <div class="hero-details">
      <p class="lead">
        Posato blocks the websites and apps you choose for a timed pause on your Mac, iPhone, Linux
        computer, or Android phone, now or on a schedule, within the <a href="#limits">limits</a> below.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">No Posato account, no analytics, and no Posato-operated server.</p>
      <p class="download">
        <a href="https://github.com/dees91/posato/releases/latest"><img src="/badges/download-for-mac.svg" width="186" height="56" alt="Download Posato for Mac" /></a>
        <a href="https://apps.apple.com/app/posato/id6812237585"><img src="/badges/download-on-the-app-store.svg" width="186" height="56" alt="Download Posato on the App Store" /></a>
      </p>
      <p class="platforms">For Mac with macOS 13 or later, Apple silicon or Intel, and iPhone with iOS 18 or later</p>
      <p class="platforms">New in 1.5: <a href="#linux-android">Linux and Android</a>, from <a href="https://github.com/dees91/posato/releases/latest">GitHub Releases</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-demo">
      <video
        class="hero-video"
        autoplay
        controls
        muted
        loop
        playsinline
        preload="metadata"
        width="1600"
        height="1000"
        poster="/media/hero-poster.jpg"
        aria-label="Posato demo: choose websites, pick 45 minutes, start a pause on a Mac, and optionally sync pause sets, sessions, and schedules with iPhone, encrypted on your device and stored in your private iCloud database"
      >
        <source src="/media/hero.mp4" type="video/mp4" media="(min-width: 701px)" />
      </video>
      <img
        class="hero-poster"
        src="/media/hero-poster.jpg"
        width="1600"
        height="1000"
        alt="Posato on a Mac reporting restrictions active, with the session end time and an option to end early"
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
    </div>
</section>

  <section class="step" aria-labelledby="choose">
    <div class="step-copy">
    <h2 id="choose">Choose what to pause</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Group what you want to pause into pause sets, such as one for work and one for evenings. A set
      holds exact website domains and, on each device, the apps you choose there. One set is the
      default; pick another when you start a pause or plan a schedule. App choices stay on the device
      where you made them.
    </p>
    </div>
    <div class="shots">
      <div class="device device-mac shot-mac">
        <div class="device-screen">
          <Image
            src={macWebsites}
            widths={[480, 636, 960, 1272]}
            sizes="(max-width: 600px) 70vw, 36rem"
            alt="Mac pause set named Focus showing the sample domains example.com and example.net"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="device device-iphone shot-iphone">
        <div class="device-screen">
          <Image
            src={iphoneWebsites}
            widths={[160, 330, 660]}
            sizes="(max-width: 600px) 24vw, 12rem"
            alt="iPhone pause set named Focus with sample website choices"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="step" aria-labelledby="start">
    <div class="step-copy">
    <h2 id="start">Start a timed pause</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Choose a pause set and a duration: a quick choice from 25 minutes to 8 hours,
      <strong>Until end of day</strong>, or any length from <strong>5 minutes to 24 hours</strong>
      (up to 23 hours 59 minutes on iPhone). Review your
      choices and start the session. Posato blocks your chosen websites and apps on that device, within the <a href="#limits">limits</a> below. The session ends at the selected time or when you deliberately end
      it early. On iPhone, restrictions can linger after the session ends. On a Mac, a one-time setup
      lets pauses and schedules start without asking for your password each time.
    </p>
    </div>
    <div class="shots">
      <div class="device device-mac shot-mac">
        <div class="device-screen">
          <Image
            src={macDuration}
            widths={[480, 636, 960, 1272]}
            sizes="(max-width: 600px) 70vw, 36rem"
            alt="Mac session setup with the pause set Focus and a 45-minute pause selected"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="device device-iphone shot-iphone">
        <div class="device-screen">
          <Image
            src={iphoneDuration}
            widths={[160, 330, 660]}
            sizes="(max-width: 600px) 24vw, 12rem"
            alt="iPhone session duration picker"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="step" aria-labelledby="schedules">
    <div class="step-copy">
    <h2 id="schedules">Plan pauses ahead</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Add a schedule with a name, a pause set, weekdays, and hours, such as weekday mornings from 9 to
      11. It starts and ends on its own on each device you set up, even with Posato's window closed or
      the iPhone app closed. Skip the next one or end one early when plans change. When pauses overlap,
      Posato pauses everything in their sets, within each device's limits, and each item stays paused
      until the last pause that includes it ends. Posato can tell you when a pause ends or when one starts on another device.
    </p>
    </div>
    <div class="shots">
      <div class="device device-mac shot-mac">
        <div class="device-screen">
          <Image
            src={macSchedules}
            widths={[480, 636, 960, 1272]}
            sizes="(max-width: 600px) 70vw, 36rem"
            alt="Mac Schedules screen with a weekday schedule named Deep work and a daily one named Evening reading"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="device device-iphone shot-iphone">
        <div class="device-screen">
          <Image
            src={iphoneSchedules}
            widths={[160, 330, 660]}
            sizes="(max-width: 600px) 24vw, 12rem"
            alt="iPhone Schedules screen with a weekday schedule named Deep work"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="muted">Screenshots are from the real apps and show sample choices.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="step" aria-labelledby="sync">
    <h2 id="sync">Share the session with iCloud</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Choose <strong>Sync with iCloud</strong> on one Mac and one iPhone signed in to the same Apple
      Account to share your pause sets with their websites, sessions, and schedules. No QR code or
      invitation is needed. Sync is best effort, so a change may arrive late or not at all. A session
      started on your iPhone blocks on the Mac only after you resume it there. Update Posato on every
      device: once one device runs Posato 1.3, devices on an earlier version stop syncing until they
      update.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="step" aria-labelledby="folder">
    <h2 id="folder">Sync through a folder</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      To link Linux, Android, or any mix of devices, keep the workspace in a folder that Dropbox,
      OneDrive, Syncthing, iCloud Drive, or another service keeps in sync. Posato writes only encrypted
      files there. The Mac and iPhone can use a folder instead of iCloud; a workspace uses one or the
      other. Create the workspace on one device, then choose <strong>Add a device</strong> there: scan
      the QR code with the other device's camera, open the shared link, or type the pairing code. The
      code works for 10 minutes. A device that joins during a pause starts pausing right away. You
      cannot remove a single device; to stop sharing with one, remove the workspace and create a new
      one in another folder.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="step" aria-labelledby="linux-android">
    <h2 id="linux-android">Linux and Android</h2>
    {/* TODO(DOCS-006): Linux and Android screenshots go here, in a .shots block like the steps above, captured by the main agent. */}
    <p class="prose">
      <strong>Linux:</strong> Posato runs on Ubuntu 24.04 or later. Download
      <code>posato_1.5.0_arm64.deb</code> for arm64 or <code>posato_1.5.0_amd64.deb</code> for x86-64
      from <a href="https://github.com/dees91/posato/releases/latest">GitHub Releases</a> and install it
      with <code>sudo apt install ./posato_1.5.0_&lt;arch&gt;.deb</code>. Then open Posato and follow
      the first run; it asks for your password once to install the pausing service.
    </p>
    <p class="prose">
      <strong>Android:</strong> Posato runs on Android 13 or later. On the phone, download
      <code>Posato-1.5.0.apk</code> from <a href="https://github.com/dees91/posato/releases/latest">GitHub Releases</a>
      and open it. When Android asks, allow installing apps from this source, then install, open
      Posato, and follow the first run, which asks for the permissions Posato needs to pause.
    </p>
    <p class="prose">To update on Linux or Android, install the newer package the same way.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="limits">
    <h2 id="limits">Limits</h2>
    <p class="prose">Posato adds deliberate friction; it is not a lock you cannot open.</p>
    <ul class="prose">
      <li>
        <strong>Mac:</strong> blocking works while Posato runs, including in the menu bar with its
        window closed. Quitting Posato stops it and new scheduled starts. Blocking needs administrator
        approval; after the one-time setup, starts no longer ask for it. Paused apps are quit, so save
        your work before a session starts. Website blocking
        covers Safari and Google Chrome Stable while they use the system proxy settings.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>iPhone:</strong> Restrictions can linger after a session ends. For sessions under 15
        minutes, they clear only when Posato is open at the end or the next time you open it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Linux and Android:</strong> websites are blocked by name, with no pause page; a browser
        with its own DNS over HTTPS bypasses it. On Linux, paused apps are ended. On Android, another
        VPN cannot run during a pause, and a paused app is covered by a block screen.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sync:</strong> Sync is best effort; a change may arrive late or not at all. If every copy of your workspace key is lost,
        synchronized data cannot be recovered.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="prose">
      Read the <a href="/limits/">full blocking and sync limits</a> for browser coverage, VPN and Private Relay behavior, resuming after sleep, folder sync and pairing codes, and data recovery.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="privacy">
    <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Posato's developer does not receive your data. Your pause sets, websites, app choices, sessions,
      and schedules stay on your devices. If you turn on iCloud sync, changes are encrypted on your device before they are
      stored in your private iCloud database. With folder sync, Posato writes only encrypted files to the folder you choose. On Mac, update checks go to GitHub Releases only after you agree.
      See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="note" aria-labelledby="availability">
    <h2 id="availability">Availability</h2>
    <p>
      Posato 1.5 for Mac is a signed and notarized download from <a href="https://github.com/dees91/posato/releases/latest">GitHub Releases</a>:
      <code>Posato-1.5.0.dmg</code> for Apple silicon and <code>Posato-1.5.0-intel.dmg</code> for an Intel Mac.
      It can check for new releases after you agree, and installing an update waits until your session has ended. To move from Posato 1.0,
      download the new version, quit Posato, and replace the application. The iPhone app is on the <a href="https://apps.apple.com/app/posato/id6812237585">App Store</a>. The Linux <code>.deb</code> packages and the Android APK are on <a href="https://github.com/dees91/posato/releases/latest">GitHub Releases</a> too. Posato targets macOS 13 or later on Apple silicon and Intel Macs, iOS 18 or later, Ubuntu 24.04 or later, and Android 13 or later; the <a href="https://github.com/dees91/posato/blob/main/docs/product/limits-and-platforms.md#supported-platforms">platform matrix</a> records what was checked, including that the Intel build was checked under Rosetta, not on an Intel Mac.
    </p>
    <p class="download">
      <a href="https://github.com/dees91/posato/releases/latest"><img src="/badges/download-for-mac.svg" width="186" height="56" alt="Download Posato for Mac" /></a>
      <a href="https://apps.apple.com/app/posato/id6812237585"><img src="/badges/download-on-the-app-store.svg" width="186" height="56" alt="Download Posato on the App Store" /></a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
